      {
        "id": 134119,
        "name": "AlexxKay",
        "username": "AlexxKay",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-28T02:19:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm with Nataraja on this.&nbsp; In order to distinguish between, for example, Ambitious Racketeer and the end-of-turn damage done by a flipped Cosmic Omnitron, you need to get into some quite complex concepts of what kind of targeting is going on.&nbsp; Conversely, just checking whether the text includes the phrase \"up to\" is simple and easy.</p><p>Are there any cards *besides* Ambitious Racketeer that share its qualities?&nbsp; And are there any cases besides Captain Cosmic that can bring out new Hero targets as a result of dealing damage?&nbsp; I suspect that this is another case where we're keeping the rules overly complex in order to support a tiny change in interpretation to a single card (or very small number of them, at any rate), and even then, only in rare circumstances.</p>",
