        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>AlexxKay wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;Conversely, just checking whether the text includes the phrase \"up to\" is simple and easy.</blockquote></div>\nChecking to see if the phrase says highest/lowest/most is not equally easy?\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not for me subjectively, since I find it unintuitive.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Not by objective complexity (measured in \"number of characters (or even words) needed to state the rule.</p>",
