        "created_at": "2015-02-28T12:00:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"AlexxKay\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> AlexxKay:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Ronway wrote:</b><br><blockquote>AlexxKay wrote:<br><blockquote>&nbsp;Conversely, just checking whether the text includes the phrase \"up to\" is simple and easy.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nChecking to see if the phrase says highest/lowest/most is not equally easy?\n</blockquote></div>\nNot for me subjectively, since I find it unintuitive.&nbsp;\n<p>Not by objective complexity (measured in \"number of characters (or even words) needed to state the rule.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>What about \"with the\"?</p>",
