      {
        "id": 134124,
        "name": "AlexxKay",
        "username": "AlexxKay",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-28T16:27:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>That seems workable.</p><p>Updating the damage dealing doc to have the following comments:</p><p>\"If the effect damages \"the N targets WITH THE (some condition)\", all the valid targets are chosen the first time we go through this step. The valid targets are *not* recalculated due to later side effects.\"</p><p>\"Conversely, if the effect damages multiple targets, but does NOT use the phrase \"WITH THE\", then you DO re-evaluate which are the valid targets every time you go through this step. For example, Taiaha can kill a Cultist, and then target the Zombie that is created in response.\"</p>",
